            <ArticleTitle>Mononitrates as monotherapy in the prophylactic treatment of angina pectoris.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>100-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article reviews the results of double-blind comparative studies on the therapeutic use of isosorbide 5-mononitrate as monotherapy in the prophylaxis of angina pectoris. Isosorbide 5-mononitrate appears at least as effective as the same dosage of isosorbide dinitrate and is probably superior to the calcium antagonists. Recent data have shown that isosorbide 5-mononitrate in a controlled-release formulation given once daily has a significantly better antianginal effect than placebo without inducing the development of tolerance.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
